1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:05,234
Today I'll show you how SOMA AI designs a folding steel trestle you can really build:

2
00:00:05,234 --> 00:00:08,760
with a folding check, a strength analysis and workshop drawings.

3
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:14,521
We use SOMA.

4
00:00:14,521 --> 00:00:18,760
It's free and open source, and you can download it at somacad.app.

5
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:21,198
SOMA itself is free.

6
00:00:21,198 --> 00:00:23,727
For SOMA AI you bring your own AI:

7
00:00:23,727 --> 00:00:26,480
a ChatGPT subscription or an API key.

8
00:00:27,450 --> 00:00:31,303
We start with a new model, saved as Folding trestle.

9
00:00:31,303 --> 00:00:33,971
In the SOMA AI tab I pick the model:

10
00:00:33,971 --> 00:00:34,860
GPT-6.1 Sol.

11
00:00:42,450 --> 00:00:45,380
For a bigger design like this, I turn the effort up to High.

12
00:00:49,550 --> 00:00:51,978
Then I describe what I need, in plain words:

13
00:00:51,978 --> 00:00:57,164
a strong trestle that folds flat for the wall, made from steel tube I can cut and weld myself.

14
00:00:57,164 --> 00:01:00,640
And I ask SOMA AI to plan it with me before it builds anything.

15
00:01:06,183 --> 00:01:08,435
SOMA AI asks four questions at once:

16
00:01:08,435 --> 00:01:13,189
the working size, the load, my tools and steel, and how thin it should fold.

17
00:01:13,189 --> 00:01:17,193
I click my answers, and for the steel I type what I really have.

18
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,941
The answer is a clear brief:

19
00:01:32,941 --> 00:01:39,223
800 millimetres high, 900 long, 300 kilos for the pair, and at most 100 millimetres thick when folded.

20
00:01:39,223 --> 00:01:47,661
It plans with my tube sizes, with positive locks and stops, and on its own it suggests a replaceable timber cap to protect the saw blade.

21
00:01:49,416 --> 00:01:51,806
Now SOMA AI builds the complete model:

22
00:01:51,806 --> 00:01:57,342
the top beam with its timber cap, both leg frames, hinges, spreaders, feet and end caps.

23
00:01:57,342 --> 00:02:03,066
It has to fold and lock without tools, with standard parts, powder-coated in signal yellow.

24
00:02:08,316 --> 00:02:15,086
SOMA AI reads its skills, writes the model, builds it eight times, and looks at its own pictures of the result along the way.

25
00:02:19,616 --> 00:02:22,560
After half an hour the trestle is complete:

26
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:31,459
130 parts, 800 millimetres high, with twin steel top rails, two braced leg frames, all in signal yellow, and a natural timber cap.

27
00:02:33,116 --> 00:02:40,286
The legs hang on sleeved hinges under the top, with washers and lock nuts, so tightening a bolt never clamps the hinge solid.

28
00:02:41,449 --> 00:02:45,216
Each side has a swing-up spreader that locks with a push-button pin.

29
00:02:45,216 --> 00:02:47,099
Opening and folding need no tools.

30
00:02:48,249 --> 00:02:51,777
The feet are welded plates with non-marking rubber soles.

31
00:02:51,777 --> 00:02:55,739
Folded, it is 96 millimetres thin, and it weighs about 18 kilos.

32
00:03:00,383 --> 00:03:01,412
Next, the folding.

33
00:03:01,412 --> 00:03:09,073
I ask for the whole sequence as an animation, from folded flat to open and locked, and back, with a collision check in every position.

34
00:03:14,316 --> 00:03:19,166
SOMA AI plans every step of the motion, writes the animation and checks it frame by frame.

35
00:03:21,616 --> 00:03:25,089
After 43 minutes the animation is in the Animation tab:

36
00:03:25,089 --> 00:03:27,741
33 seconds, with a caption for every step.

37
00:03:33,216 --> 00:03:36,034
It starts folded flat, as it hangs on the wall.

38
00:03:36,034 --> 00:03:41,249
Swing the carrying latch clear, open the legs, and lock both spreaders with their pins.

39
00:03:41,249 --> 00:03:44,786
Then the same way back, until the frames lie flat together.

40
00:03:59,916 --> 00:04:03,025
It checked all 991 frames with the exact shapes:

41
00:04:03,025 --> 00:04:04,320
no unwanted overlap.

42
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:09,760
The smallest gap between the two leg frames is 1.45 millimetres, at the folded feet.

43
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:13,646
On the way it also corrected the holes for the locking pins.

44
00:04:15,383 --> 00:04:16,762
Now the important part:

45
00:04:16,762 --> 00:04:17,541
will it hold?

46
00:04:17,541 --> 00:04:25,396
I ask for SOMA's strength analysis with 150 kilos on one trestle, also near one end and with someone leaning sideways on the board.

47
00:04:25,396 --> 00:04:29,113
If the safety factor is below 2, it should improve the design.

48
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,682
First it asks one question:

49
00:04:38,682 --> 00:04:41,691
how hard does someone lean on the board?

50
00:04:41,691 --> 00:04:45,980
I pick a firm lean, 300 newtons, about 30 kilos sideways.

51
00:04:46,930 --> 00:04:52,334
SOMA AI sets up the load cases and lets the feet lift or slide, instead of pinning them to the floor.

52
00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:57,845
The hinges with their small details are hard to mesh, so it simplifies them and runs study after study.

53
00:04:58,795 --> 00:05:01,467
After five and a half hours, its answer.

54
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:04,340
The weak spot it found is not in the steel:

55
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:09,083
with the lean, the trestle could tip too easily, a margin of only 1.75.

56
00:05:09,083 --> 00:05:12,690
So it widened the legs and moved them nearer the ends.

57
00:05:12,690 --> 00:05:16,765
Now the margin is 2.12, and it still folds to 98 millimetres.

58
00:05:17,715 --> 00:05:20,256
In the Analysis tab are all its studies.

59
00:05:20,256 --> 00:05:22,225
Here is the case I asked about:

60
00:05:22,225 --> 00:05:25,845
150 kilos near the end, plus the lean, on the welded top.

61
00:05:28,417 --> 00:05:32,770
The lowest safety factor in this study is 2.5, above the required 2.

62
00:05:32,770 --> 00:05:34,691
Red would mark steel below it:

63
00:05:34,691 --> 00:05:35,587
there is none.

64
00:05:36,537 --> 00:05:40,001
The weakest area is where the top rail joins the hinge saddle.

65
00:05:40,001 --> 00:05:41,397
And SOMA AI stays honest:

66
00:05:41,397 --> 00:05:45,587
that peak changes with the mesh, so it does not call the trestle confirmed.

67
00:05:45,587 --> 00:05:48,827
Check the welds and do a proof test before you rely on it.

68
00:05:50,277 --> 00:05:52,058
Later I open the model again.

69
00:05:52,058 --> 00:05:58,567
Under Earlier conversations the trestle conversation is still there, and SOMA AI goes on where it stopped.

70
00:06:01,010 --> 00:06:02,537
Now the workshop package:

71
00:06:02,537 --> 00:06:09,620
drawings of the welded frames with all lengths, angles, holes and weld symbols, plus a cut list and a shopping list.

72
00:06:12,877 --> 00:06:19,167
SOMA AI lays out the sheets, looks at its own drawings as pictures and fixes what it finds, like a reversed angle label.

73
00:06:20,177 --> 00:06:22,627
After 57 minutes the package is ready:

74
00:06:22,627 --> 00:06:24,561
35 sheets in the Drawings tab.

75
00:06:24,561 --> 00:06:26,947
I make the column wider to read them.

76
00:06:28,110 --> 00:06:33,447
Each welded frame has its own sheet with lengths, holes and proposed weld symbols:

77
00:06:33,447 --> 00:06:36,505
two millimetre fillet welds, numbered W1 to W5.

78
00:06:37,743 --> 00:06:40,063
Every tube has a cut and drill drawing.

79
00:06:40,063 --> 00:06:43,633
The legs are cut at 24 degrees, with every hole dimensioned.

80
00:06:44,877 --> 00:06:50,285
The cut list gives every tube and sleeve with its length and mitre angle, for one trestle and for the pair.

81
00:06:51,543 --> 00:06:52,921
And the shopping lists:

82
00:06:52,921 --> 00:06:57,113
steel, timber and rubber, then the bolts, pins and other bought parts.

83
00:07:02,877 --> 00:07:04,472
SOMA AI stays honest here too:

84
00:07:04,472 --> 00:07:09,788
the package is marked review only, because the sleeve welds and the full load rating are still open.

85
00:07:09,788 --> 00:07:12,127
The last check before the first cut is mine.

86
00:07:13,077 --> 00:07:13,762
Here it is:

87
00:07:13,762 --> 00:07:20,241
a folding steel trestle, planned, built, checked and drawn by SOMA AI, in about eight hours of its work.

88
00:07:21,777 --> 00:07:24,651
From an idea to a design you can build.

89
00:07:24,651 --> 00:07:26,788
SOMA is free and open source:

90
00:07:26,788 --> 00:07:28,778
download it at somacad.app.
